{
  "about": [
    "The wiki chat's vectors (contracts/wiki.contract.json `chat`, `docs.follow`, `docs.versions`; docs/wiki-contract.md",
    "§28–§30; docs/wiki-chat-design.md §3–§8): what a card shows and offers in each state, the line under an applied card,",
    "the round button's look, what adds to the Wiki's waiting count, why a follow job waits, which two jobs of a space may",
    "run at once, which sections a card rewrites, the sentence-level comparison See changes draws, what an attachment line",
    "says, what a message's wikiContext may hold, and the Docs rows of Activity.",
    "",
    "src/shared/src/wikiChatContract.spec.ts runs every case through src/shared/src/wikiChat.ts, the functions the server",
    "computes its states and counts with. OrbitKit mirrors the client half (the card, the line, the button, the counts,",
    "the notes and the rows) and reads this same file; the web reads the shared functions themselves. Plain JSON, no",
    "comments and no TypeScript, so both ends read one answer. The words are the contract's `chat.copy`, `docs.follow.copy`",
    "and `docs.versions.copy`, which the spec holds to WIKI_CHAT_COPY.",
    "",
    "A card here is { kind, state, undoable, rewrite }: the card read's fields these derivations use (contract",
    "`chat.drafts.read`). `facts` are what `state` is derived from (contract `chat.drafts.derivation`)."
  ],
